<title>RUSSIA: Russia-Belarus Slavneft 96 oil output slips.</title>
<headline>Russia-Belarus Slavneft 96 oil output slips.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian-Belarussian joint venture Slavneft produced 12.9 million tonnes of oil in 1996, down from 13.2 million tonnes in 1995, it said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It also said output was expected to drop further in 1997 to 11.9 million tonnes. Slavneft's main production unit is the Russia-based Megionneftegaz.  </p>
<p>Slavneft refined a total of 12 million tonnes of oil in 1996, down over 21 percent from year-ago levels.</p>
<p>Its total crude oil exports last year to all destinations were 6.0 million tonnes, down 10.4 percent on 1995's level. It blamed the drop on problems with access to the Transneft state pipeline monopoly's pipeline system.</p>
<p>Slavneft gave the following data for its three refineries --</p>
<p>	    SLAVNEFT REFINERIES' OUTPUT (IN MILLION TONNES)</p>
<p>	     Yaroslavnefteorgsintez   Mendeleev	Mozyrsk</p>
<p>			 1996   1995     1996   1995    1996   1995</p>
<p>Refined oil	  6.59   9.37     0.06   0.19    5.32   5.63</p>
<p>All gasoline	 1.08   1.42     ----   ----    0.95   1.02</p>
<p>(of which</p>
<p> car gasoline)     0.95   1.40     ----   ----    0.03   0.04</p>
<p>Jet fuel	     0.52   0.60     ----   ----    0.28   0.22</p>
<p>Diesel		 1.51   2.17     0.02   0.05    1.38   1.56</p>
<p>Heavy fuel oil     2.43   3.90     ----   0.03    2.19   2.51</p>
<p>Slavneft is one of around a dozen vertically-integrated oil</p>
<p>companies in Russia.</p>
<p>--Mike Collett-White, Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
